# DECK 05 — SCAFFOLD. Titles, demo targets and `notes:` stubs in place; TODO prose to write.
# Sources: docs/documents/chapter (the document model), docs/documents/marklower (the prose format and its
# delegations). Series rules: ../.yo/body.yo.
!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
Chapters and marklower
description: Why the prose format refuses headings — and what carries them instead
- A document is a node
  notes: |
    TODO — open examples/60-simple-chapter.yo. A chapter is a fully omni node: its
    own value is the TITLE, `description` is keyed, and every keyless entry is a body
    element — prose, a picture, or a subchapter, in one ordered stream.
  - |
    A chapter's **title is the node's own value**; its body is one ordered stream of
    chunks and subchapters, in the order the author wrote them.
- Marklower — a notch below Markdown
  notes: |
    TODO — docs/documents/marklower. Five constructs and no others: bold, italic, strike, code, math,
    a link. Everything else passes through.
  - !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
    header: [Syntax, Meaning]
    - - '`**bold**`, `*italic*`, `~~strike~~`'
      - the usual runs
    - - '`` `code` ``, `$$math$$`'
      - atomic — never re-read as markup
    - - '`[label](target)`'
      - a link — *points at* the target
- No headings, on purpose
  notes: |
    TODO — the design argument: a `##` buried in a chunk cannot become a subchapter that
    the tree lists, that a pointer addresses, or that an edit moves. So block structure
    belongs to the chapter, and marklower keeps only what a sentence needs.
  - |
    A `##` inside prose can never be **navigated to, pointed at, or moved**. So structure
    is the chapter's job, and marklower stays inline-only.
- Tables and lists are nodes
  notes: |
    TODO — examples/61-table.yo. Markdown draws a table out of pipes; here the grid
    is a yamlover node and only the cells are prose. Same for bullet and numbered lists.
  - |
    TODO — one sentence on delegation: the structure marklower refuses to own.
- Links across the tree
  notes: |
    TODO — examples/69-marklower-links.yo. A link target is a sigiled pointer in the same
    space the tree and the URL navigate (docs/documents/marklower/link-targets), so prose can
    point anywhere.
  - |
    TODO — one sentence.
- Embeds
  notes: |
    TODO — no embed token: embedding is structural, a body element — a `*` pointer to a
    media member, or a chunk whose whole text is one media URL. Show a picture inlined
    from a sibling file.
  - |
